            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="INTRODUCTION" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Asthma is the most prevalent chronic illness in children and has been related to psychological aspects involved in its evolution.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To understand the types of relational patterns observed in families of children with this illness.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHOD" NlmCategory="METHODS">Qualitative analysis through intentional sample of children between the ages of 4 to 15 years with asthma and other mixed populations.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS AND CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The analysis shows families with diffuse limits between its members, tendency towards amalgamation, high levels of anxiety, and the presence of parental and parental-offspring conflicts.</AbstractText>
